    "result_text": "I agree with the finding and addressed it. The domain-extraction sequence (`normalize` \u2192 `lastIndexOf('@')` \u2192 guard \u2192 `substring`) was inlined in both `isDisposable` and `isDisposableAdjacent`, in the class whose javadoc says these notions should \"stay defined in one place.\"\n\nI extracted a private `domainOf(String email)` returning the domain or `null`, and both methods now call it:\n- `isDisposable` \u2192 `domain != null && DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS.contains(domain)`\n- `isDisposableAdjacent` \u2192 present/valid guard, then `domain != null && !DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS.contains(domain) && DISPOSABLE_BASE_LABELS.contains(baseLabel(domain))`\n\n\"The domain of an email\" now sits as one defined notion alongside `baseLabel`, matching the class's design intent. Behaviour is unchanged and the full test suite is green (1/1 passing).",
